# -n -v DIR where a soname's path is a regular file: the file is left alone and reported.
name: ldconfig -n -v leaves a regular file at a soname path
clause: s31_2_g_4
# The reference is Debian's wrapper script, which execs /sbin/ldconfig.real: its program name is normalised.
normalise: /sbin/ldconfig.real => ldconfig
normalise: ldconfig.real => ldconfig
command: ldconfig
env: LC_ALL=C
arg: -n
arg: -v
arg: @ROOT@/lib
elf: lib/libreg.so.7.0 soname=libreg.so.7
file: lib/libreg.so.7
| a regular file
status: exit 0
stdout:
| @ROOT@/lib: (from <cmdline>:0)
| \tlibreg.so.7 -> libreg.so.7.0
stderr:
| ldconfig: @ROOT@/lib/libreg.so.7 is not a symbolic link
|
